# TypeScript Standards

- Prefer explicit, domain-focused types for public function inputs/outputs.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` with narrowing when type is uncertain.
- Keep functions small and single-purpose; extract helpers instead of deep nesting.
- Handle async failures with meaningful errors; do not silently swallow exceptions.
- Reuse existing validators/schemas (for example Zod) before introducing new validation styles.

## Example

```typescript
// Avoid
async function getDoctor(id: any) {
  try { return await repo.findById(id); } catch { return null; }
}

// Preferred
async function getDoctor(id: string) {
  try {
    return await repo.findById(id);
  } catch (error) {
    throw new Error("Failed to load doctor record");
  }
}
```
